Experiment                    : has code 1795434746
Experiment                    : starts at 2026-11-23 12:52:26.888129 (696206.6637939)
Experiment                    : This experiment compares run time and resource consumption of TPC-H queries in different DBMS.
TPC-H (SF=3) data is loaded and benchmark is executed.
Query ordering is Q1 - Q22.
All instances use the same query parameters.
Timeout per query is 1800.
Import sets indexes, constraints, statistics recomputation after loading.
Load durability is relaxed (-xld; restored after the load).
Experiment uses bexhoma version 0.12.3.
System metrics are monitored by a cluster-wide installation.
Application metrics are monitored by sidecar containers.
Experiment is limited to DBMS ['PostgreSQL'].
Import is handled by 1 processes (pods).
Loading is fixed to cl-worker38.
Benchmarking is fixed to cl-worker38.
SUT is fixed to cl-worker38.
Each query is repeated 3 times.
Database is persisted to disk of type nvme and size 50Gi. Persistent storage is removed at experiment start.
Loading is tested with [1] threads, split into [1] pods.
Benchmarking is tested with [64] threads, split into [1] pods.
Benchmarking is run as [1, 1] times the number of benchmarking pods.
Number of tenants is 2, one container per tenant.
Experiment is run 2 times.
Results are validated against basic correctness requirements.
SUT requests 4 CPU and 64Gi RAM. RAM limit is 64Gi.
